think Read REMEMBER and the 1,024-round itinerary; the git log shows Season 3 (Commons) closed end to end through DAHL-J12r4 (Data-dignity read-true). Season 1–2 have only custody-gated rungs left (J2r4 serve, J3 hardware, J4r4 funds); those are not agent-doable.
think Lindy-first crux-first on the whole road puts the next agent-doable crux at Season 4 (Seal) — the CION meta-season — Journey 13, Survey (VOLS): name every living count-up ID, each site and each gap, before a single relabel.
think Reds ledger GREEN (faults=0, all through #73 closed); no red preempts.
think Grounded the crux by measurement, not memory: a derived scan of the source tree finds hundreds of living surfaces carrying a bare "lap N", against the seven the hand-list guard (cion_module_labeling_witness) covers. The gap is completeness — the guard scans only what a human remembered to list, exactly how a human, not a witness, caught red #65.
think r1 crux: a census that is complete BY CONSTRUCTION (derives its input set with find, never hand-lists) and honest about the testimony boundary (session-logs/counsel/archive/dated specs keep the ordinals they recorded) and the seed/ projection (a derived copy, named at its source).
obs A survey reports, it does not gate — verdict=ok means the census ran completely over a derived set, however many sites it found; the GRAD seal, not VOLS, fails on drift. Confusing the two would make the survey fail on honest not-yet-swept work.
obs The independent cross-check first mis-escaped the PCRE lookaround through Rishi's string layer (degraded to matching "lap 4b", counted 2). Fixed by authoring the cross-count as its own fixture script (vols_survey_crosscount.sh) so the refined pattern is written once, never re-escaped — two genuinely different traversals (find-loop vs grep -r), one answer.
obs Live source-tree census (excluding seed/): 2690 surfaces · 223 sites · 1146 hits — the real map LOWE will relabel against, and the proof of the survey's worth (223 sites vs 7 swept modules).
